  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Croatia Disaster Preparedness and Resilience Development Policy Loan with a Catastrophe Deferred Drawdown Option (Cat DDO)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Program Development Objective is to strengthen Croatia&apos;s disaster preparedness and resilience by enhancing institutional capacity at the national level and across strategic sectors, and increasing financial resilience.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The development objective of Disaster Preparedness and Resilience Development Policy Loan with a Catastrophe Deferred Drawdown Option Program is to strengthen Croatia&apos;s disaster preparedness and resilience by enhancing institutional capacity at the national level and across strategic sectors, and increasing financial resilience.  Accordingly, Pillar 1&#x2014;Strengthening institutional capacity for disaster preparedness and resilience, will support foundational reforms that increase the disaster preparedness of critical infrastructure and services, and that build institutional capacity for climate adaptation (CA). Pillar 2&#x2014;Enhancing disaster preparedness and climate resilience in key economic sectors, will support reforms that address vulnerabilities and foster sustainable development in the energy, tourism, and housing sectors. Pillar 3&#x2014;Strengthening the financial resilience of businesses and households, will advance reforms in the insurance and social protection sectors to enhance coping and recovery capacity for disaster and climate impacts. These reforms are complemented by the Cat DDO as a contingent financing mechanism that can supplement budget reserves and enhance fiscal resilience in case of major disasters.  The Cat DDO supports GoC&apos;s efforts to strengthen its framework and capacity for disaster preparedness and resilience, improving public sector service and impact, and private action. Competitiveness, resilience of the economy, and better quality of life for citizens are key commitments in the GoC&apos;s program (2024&#x2013;2028). Croatia has a well-established DRM framework covering all emergencies with health-related emergencies covered under the public health preparedness system. The Cat DDO leverages and complements the WBG&apos;s program in Croatia. Ongoing operations finance the upgrading of public infrastructure to meet modern building codes and safety and energy efficiency standards. The Cat DDO is consistent with the Maximizing Finance for Development (MFD) approach, being MFD-enabling and Private Capital Enabled (PCE). This operation is fully aligned with Croatia&apos;s national climate commitments and the Paris Agreement.</narrative>
  </description>
